    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.move\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11.x\n\n### Description\n\nmini.move behave strangely with escape characters, like `^[` or `^V`, etc...\n(inserted using `<C-v><esc>` for example).\n\nThis is totally fine if there is no fix for it, it's a very niche problem.\nI just wanted to document it at least so people might be less confused..\n\n### Reproduction\n\n- In visual mode selecting any number of character and moving hover this kind of char will simply erase it.\n\nI have been re-implementing this plugin's core logic for myself and I now believe its due to pasting just to the right of the ^ part.\nso like \n```\n^[\n ┗pasting here erase the whole thing\n```\n\n- It gets weirder, in visual-block mode when moving a regular char, it will push \n  everything after the escape char, like if it collided on it!\n  But only when moving to the right.  \n\nExample:\n```\nI text\nI ^[sometext\nI text\n\n textI\n     I^[sometext\n textI\n```\nI am very puzzled by this behavior.\n",
