            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nI can partially reproduce: only the \"It gets weirder\" blockwise visual selection part. The reason this happens is because `^]` occupies two cells while cells above and below are two separate characters. So it seems like pasting step of the move tries to insert the text in a way that doesn't want to split the `^]` part of the symbol. Hence it moves it to the right. The solution here is to move by two cells in one go: press `2` followed by `<M-l>`.\n\nI can not reproduce any weird behavior in charwise selection. Here is the demo:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d85fcb15-d6f7-4b77-8f98-25d37383e79b\n\nClosing as working as intended.",
